WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. 
(Take whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! 
Are gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.870
Um... I'm in a great deal of pain.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.160
What hurts?

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.170
I hate to say it in front of ladies,

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:51.920
but it's my bottom.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.170
Well, I guess that's part 
of your training, too.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.170
You can be so heartless, Miss Pacifica...

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.390
Why are we taking an untraveled 
road like this, anyway?

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:03.470
It's not like you had to take 
the same road as us, Leo.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:05.180
You truly are cruel, Miss Pacifica...

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:10.190
I mean, I've already lost 
my path in life overall!

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:13.400
I suppose that it wouldn't be 
training if you didn't suffer.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.760
That's so cruel!

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.130
Shannon.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:29.710
"Fanfare for the Unforgiven Man"

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.720
We should have taken this 
road in the first place...

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.470
Still, I wonder if something has happened?

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.680
Look at all of those Royal Forces troops.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:46.720
I'll go ask.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:48.390
Shannon...

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:49.730
It'll be okay.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:51.650
All right, move along!

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:52.230
Next!

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.940
They say that the Scrapped 
Princess is still alive.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.860
My, how horrible...

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.650
Did she take this road?

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.860
You people!

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.410
Don't fall for a bunch of crazy rumors!

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.580
That's got nothing to 
do with this checkpoint!

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:05.780
Hurry up and move your cart!

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.080
I've got it!

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.580
When I asked them why they've 
put up this checkpoint, they...

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:14.080
Miss Pacifica?

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.880
You carry around such outfits 
with you, big brother?

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.220
Pretty much.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.090
Oh, I get it!

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:24.430
You're all traveling performers, am I right?

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:25.780
Let's ditch this guy.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:26.220
Good idea.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:31.230
What cruel siblings...

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.740
Think she looks like the drawing, Corporal?

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:44.990
Well, they do say that she's traveling 
with a black-haired man and woman...

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.000
Please don't leave me behind!

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.460
Are you putting on a show or 
something in the next town?

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:55.810
Who are you?

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.500
My name is Leopold Skorpus.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:02.510
I'd like to be of assistance 
to this traveling troupe!

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:05.510
That's Baron Skorpus' family crest.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:07.560
Let me help you!

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.430
I'll even play the horse's legs! Anything!

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.020
Go ahead and pass, sir.

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:12.020
Thank you!

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.720
Come now, let's be off!

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:16.520
Move along!

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.150
Thank you!

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:31.080
He certainly saved us back there.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.250
I guess even morons have their uses.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.750
Hey, I guess you've got a little 
raison d'être in you, after all!

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:55.020
This is so comfy! It's been 
so long since I've seen a bed!

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:57.730
They said that they even have 
a jungle-themed bath here.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:58.860
That sounds neat!

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:07.320
There's even a church on 
the outskirts of town.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.240
We just slipped through their checkpoint,

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:11.370
so I think their morale 
will be low for a while.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:15.410
Hey, let's go out and get something 
great for dinner tonight!

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:16.200
Forget it.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.290
Why not?

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:18.080
We've got no money.

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.250
It's all we can do to pay for our rooms.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:23.510
You're kidding!

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:26.590
You're the one who said you 
wanted to sleep in a bed!

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:29.280
You're a young fogey, Shannon!

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:30.800
I, however, am a young maiden!

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:33.310
No maiden spouts the garbage that you do.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:34.350
This one does!

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:39.400
You want me to tie you up and hang 
you from somebody's front eaves?

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.070
Folks like you sleep really 
well when they're strung up.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:43.120
What's that supposed to mean?

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.820
We aren't curing meats, you know.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:48.160
Oh, shut up. I wish you'd turn 
into some dried food for a while.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:50.740
Like flounder?

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.240
Or a puffer fish?

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.290
Why, you little...

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.290
You got a problem?!

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.710
Let go of my face!

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.710
I'm so sorry for the racket.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:58.440
That's fine.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:01.460
As long as you don't dirty the 
rooms or smash the furniture,

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:05.000
you can beat each other up or 
dance in a circle for all I...

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:11.180
That's great! I love that back talk!

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:13.480
I think we'll be friends!

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:16.020
I'm Pacifica!

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:17.680
Um...

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:18.710
Winia.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:22.230
Have you finished cleaning the guest rooms?

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:24.320
Hm? Yes, sir.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:25.700
C'mon, Winia!

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.280
Will you show us around town?

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:30.240
And then tell us where we 
can find some work, okay?

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.320
Hey!

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.260
Let's go!

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:33.280
Um, I...

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:35.700
Go on.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:39.620
But I haven't changed the sheets yet...

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:40.790
That's okay, that's okay!

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:43.380
You can leave that to the old geezer!

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.750
You want <i>me </i>to do it?!

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:45.670
C'mon!

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.560
Hurry, hurry!

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.140
Jobs, huh?

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:54.180
Well, it might be a good way 
to fool people and blend in.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.460
That's true.

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:58.060
In that case, you work hard, too, Shannon.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.110
This is part of my training, too!

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.730
That's Taurus over there.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.900
We apparently overlooked 
them at the checkpoint,

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:12.110
but the group almost certainly 
snuck into that town.

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:14.410
The main body of the Royal Forces

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:17.240
doesn't want to get involved 
in any unpleasantness.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:21.170
I guess they think that it's the Special 
Forces' job to get their hands dirty.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:24.590
At any rate, halfhearted measures 
won't work against these people.

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:27.340
We'll go scout out the 
Scrapped Princess' location.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:31.040
Sure. I'll carry out the mission this time.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:33.390
Personally. No matter what it takes.

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:36.180
That's so cute!

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:39.060
Say, how do you think this 
would look in your room, Winia?

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.390
Why don't you buy it?

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:44.900
We're in the middle of a trip.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:46.900
Oh, that's right.

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:56.070
I... I've never set foot 
outside this town of Taurus.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:08:00.580
I work in that inn from dawn to dusk,

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:03.080
doing nothing but looking after 
people who are passing through.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.040
That sounds nice.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:10.090
What's so good about a life like that?

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.890
Well, I think...

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:14.090
I'm jealous of you, Winia.

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:18.590
Miss Pacifica!

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:20.770
Leo?

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.100
Did you manage to find 
lodgings somewhere, too?

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:25.480
No, I'm borrowing the barn of a local house.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:27.110
Oh, so you're broke, too!

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:28.830
Truth be told,

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:32.610
I'd love to be able to buy you, 
my betrothed, a single rose.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:36.030
Hey, since when are we engaged?!

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:39.120
Oh, perhaps that was 
brazen of me... Oh, dear!

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:42.120
"Oh, dear"?! Is that all you've got to say?

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.180
Why am I stuck doing this?

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:49.630
Oops, I gotta smooth out this end, too...

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:54.340
Sorry, miss, I've got all 
the help I need right now.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:55.130
Oh, you do?

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:58.430
Let's try somewhere else.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:01.970
Too bad, the uniforms at 
this cafe were cute...

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.590
Raquel, what's the matter?

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:09.720
That's so cute!

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:15.190
Announcing our new Mr. Soopie buns!

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:16.700
Would you like to try a sample?

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:19.300
They're really delicious!

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:20.700
Would you like to try some?

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:23.200
Get your Mr. Soopie buns!

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:25.780
Would you like one?

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:28.710
Get your Mr. Soopie buns!

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:31.430
Would you like a sample?

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:40.430
Geez, the customers run away 
when they see this thing!

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:42.970
But why? Look at how cute it is...

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.600
You people are lifesavers.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:49.560
I haven't been able to find many part-time 
workers willing to wear that suit.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:51.230
I suppose not...

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:56.190
We plan to expand our product line, 
centering around Mr. Soopie there.

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:59.200
Mr. Soopie danishes. Cream buns. Jam buns.

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:02.200
They all seem to look the same...

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:05.330
Go on, now! Advertise them even more!

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:09.250
Let's give it our best, shall we?

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.790
Would you like to try our line of buns?

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:15.800
Would you like a Mr. Soopie bun?

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:18.300
Would you like a sample?!

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:20.560
We're not doing well...

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:22.300
Okay, then!

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:24.810
Hello, there!

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:26.770
H-Hello?

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.310
Would you like to try one?

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:30.810
S-Sure...

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.310
Hello, there!

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:34.070
Hello!

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:36.280
Would you like to try one?

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:38.780
Maybe I'll try one, too!

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:45.790
It's delicious!

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:46.980
Gimme one!

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:47.750
Here!

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:48.550
Me, too!

00:10:48.550 --> 00:10:49.290
Here you are!

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:52.790
All right, this is getting on my nerves...

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:55.300
Would you like one? Would you like one?

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:00.410
Maybe I'll try one, too!

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:03.500
See? Look, look! Look!

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:04.850
Look, I'm eating it!

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:07.050
Look! C'mon, look!

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:08.930
My jaw fell off!

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:11.850
Sheesh!

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:14.170
Miss Pacifica, you certainly hate to lose!

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:17.820
Did you like that, Winia?

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:22.110
I thought you looked like a fool, that's all.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.300
Let's go, Winia!

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:27.620
I'm gonna look for a different job.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.960
Then I will, too.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:35.680
Would you like one?

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:38.650
Mr. Soopie buns are delicious!

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:39.130
Excuse me.

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:40.720
Yes?

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:44.590
Have you seen a blonde-haired girl 
with eyes like a cat's around here?

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:46.420
Who are you?

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:48.640
Wait, don't tell me you're 
a rival for her affections?!

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:53.100
Just who are you?! Who?!

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:53.100
Hey! What are you doing?

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:53.650
Dennis!

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:57.020
I've found out where she is.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:02.530
Hey! Wait a minute!

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:04.420
Ow, ow, ow...

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:16.500
Hey, now!

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.210
You've got to put your back 
into it when you're scrubbing!

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:23.220
I don't want to hear it! If you're 
gonna bother me, get lost!

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:24.510
What're you talking about?!

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:28.020
I'm doing my job and checking 
to see how hot the water is!

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:31.560
Do you actually have 
something worth hiding now?

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:36.020
I'm so glad that we've found a place to work.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:38.900
It just means that you can stay for free.

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:42.440
I heard that you recommended 
us to the innkeeper.

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:44.070
I didn't really do anything.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:45.530
Thank you.

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:50.580
Boy, that was a good sweat!

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:52.540
Are you done cleaning the bath?

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.580
My brother Shannon's doing it.

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:59.290
So you're just having your 
brother do everything for you...

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:01.460
Maybe that's his lot in life...

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.300
What's that supposed to mean?

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:06.380
I'm not really cut out for manual labor.

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:07.550
More importantly, how about some tea?

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:10.820
I have a cake that I got from that bakery!

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:11.810
Let's eat it!

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:14.560
Winia, go ahead and have some tea, okay?

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.940
Thanks, Raquel.

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:18.990
But I...

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:20.570
It's okay, it's okay!

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:22.050
C'mon, hurry!

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:31.950
I've never seen Winia be 
so open with anyone before.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:35.770
Ever since her parents died,

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:38.950
I've hardly ever seen her so much as smile.

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.710
Ta-dah!

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:47.930
That baker sure has strange tastes...

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:50.100
I've always thought that, too.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:51.720
I bet!

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:57.230
Let's get cutting!

00:13:58.270 --> 00:13:59.020
Slice!

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.000
What in the world am I doing here?

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:07.530
Would you like some Mr. Soopie buns?!

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:13.540
So, you and your uncle run this 
inn all by yourselves, Winia?

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:14.910
Yes.

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:17.080
You're so amazing, Winia.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:19.420
You can even cook. You've 
really got your act together.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:20.540
I wouldn't go that far...

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:23.210
I mean, if you weren't here,

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:25.800
the Big Bear Inn couldn't 
stay in business, right?

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:30.930
I... I'm just repaying the man 
who took me in, that's all.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:33.310
All I know how to do is work hard.

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:35.860
Still, that's really amazing.

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:39.100
Not only can't I do anything at all,

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:42.360
the world would apparently 
be better off without me.

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:50.030
Sorry, I'm just grumbling.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:54.020
I can't really do that in 
front of Shannon or Raquel.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:15:00.040
When I get angry at myself, I clean things.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:02.760
I'm not really sure why, though...

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:04.040
Is that strange?

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:07.050
Next time, I'll give that a try, too.

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:10.620
Sure, and you can get your 
brother to do it for you again.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:14.550
What?

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:18.060
Wow, you've got really pretty eyes, Winia!

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:23.230
That's amazing! I can see myself in them!

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:26.300
Hey, you're right! I can see myself, too!

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:32.950
Maybe I can stay in this town for a while...

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:43.950
Well, that should just about do it.

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:47.270
You'll make someone a fine wife.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.130
I don't want to hear that from some kid.

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:56.140
Of course, I bet that isn't the real you.

00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:58.810
How can you tell?

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:01.100
Because I can't sense your presence, I guess.

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:04.560
With illusions, I guess you can 
take whatever form you want.

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:07.650
Anyway, I wasn't the one 
who decided on this form.

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:10.920
I came here today to warn you.

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:14.160
New assassins have come.

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:19.700
And here I thought we'd be able 
to take it easy for a while...

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:21.660
Well, thanks for the warning.

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:24.790
Even though I have no idea who you are.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:27.460
You can call me Zefiris.

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:29.460
Zefiris?

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:32.290
That is the name I was given.

00:16:32.290 --> 00:16:33.720
Please remember it.

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:43.150
I'm sorry.

00:16:43.150 --> 00:16:44.980
We're gonna have to leave in a hurry.

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:47.090
Is it always like this?

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:51.600
It just seems more like you're 
on the run than on a trip.

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:55.360
I thought we'd be able 
to stay a while longer,

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:56.660
but I guess I was being naive.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:59.620
If you want to stay, why don't you?

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.440
I do.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:05.800
I mean, I might have finally 
made a friend here...

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:07.700
I want you to, too.

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:13.130
Winia...

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:35.960
How do you do?

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:40.660
Can I help you?

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:43.660
You know Shannon Cassul, don't you?

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:46.250
Huh? No, I...

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:49.670
Now, now. You shouldn't lie.

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.210
Let go! No!

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:53.380
Let go of me! Winia!

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.130
What do you think you're...

00:17:57.490 --> 00:17:58.800
Uncle!

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:05.060
I'm going to use you as bait.

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:08.810
Hurry it up.

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:12.280
I don't want to make any 
trouble for this inn.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.320
Winia... She's been...

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:21.570
Innkeeper!

00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:23.240
What happened to Winia?!

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:25.040
She was taken away...

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:26.040
By who?!

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:28.280
A strange boy in a military uniform...

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:33.210
What's this "Arwen Gorge"?

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:36.550
A valley of glass that's out 
beyond the north gate...

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:39.600
But it's a fairly dangerous place...

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:43.040
Wait! I'll go get some youngsters from town!

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:44.220
I'll go by myself.

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:48.230
Going after him in numbers 
would put Winia in danger.

00:18:48.570 --> 00:18:50.680
Rest assured, I'll bring her back.

00:18:53.680 --> 00:18:54.730
Wait, big brother!

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:56.570
I'll go, too!

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:58.240
Forget it.

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:01.990
Have dinner waiting, okay?

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:03.780
Enough for two.

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:05.620
Sure.

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:29.400
Are you awake?

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:33.520
Who are you?

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:35.650
You can call me Chris.

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:38.070
Don't worry.

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:40.010
You might make it home safe and sound

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:42.160
if the Guardian doesn't do anything foolish.

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:44.450
What? What are you talking about?

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:47.450
Oh, that's right. You don't know.

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:52.500
This is a story about a kingdom.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:56.130
There, the queen gave birth to 
fine twins, a boy and a girl.

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:59.460
However, the people of the 
castle were atremble with fear.

00:20:00.310 --> 00:20:04.970
This was because there had been a divine 
revelation regarding those twins.

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:09.470
"Of the twins delivered 
from the queen's womb,

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:11.430
slay the girl-child immediately.

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:16.270
She will give rise to mountains 
of corpses and rivers of blood.

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:17.900
On the destined day,

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:20.100
she will become the poison 
which will destroy this world."

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:23.450
The Revelation of Saint Grendel?

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:26.740
They're prophecies delivered 
once a year at Grendel,

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:29.040
the holy land of the Church of Mauser.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:31.330
Their accuracy is nearly perfect.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:34.860
Since then, fifteen years have passed.

00:20:34.860 --> 00:20:37.250
And one day, the royal 
family happened to discover

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:41.350
that the princess who was believed to have 
been scrapped was, in fact, still alive.

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:43.360
You don't mean...

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:45.970
It's Pacifica?

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:48.970
Fascinating story, isn't it?

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets sail. 
(The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.410 --> 00:22:46.420
"Next Time"

00:22:34.400 --> 00:22:37.410
Winia has learned Pacifica 
is the Scrapped Princess.

00:22:37.410 --> 00:22:40.730
Shannon heads to the glass 
valley to rescue her.

00:22:40.730 --> 00:22:43.630
And Pacifica makes dinner in the hopes that

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:45.940
her brother will come home safe.

00:22:45.940 --> 00:22:47.710
Next time on <i>Scrapped Princess</i>,

00:22:47.710 --> 00:22:49.360
"Concerto of Meetings and Partings."

00:22:49.360 --> 00:22:50.430
Please tune in!
